Chapter: ListLiteralTooLarge

 Pins CDX9004, and pins its position. A list literal costs one LIVE local
 per element: the emitter evaluates every element into its own local and
 holds all of them until the buffer is filled afterwards. A local is
 addressed by a number bounded to 65535 and spill slots start at 32, so
 max-list-literal-elems elements is the ceiling and this literal is one
 past it. Before the check existed this died in an invalid opcode inside
 alloc-local with no CDX code and nothing in the log to say what was wrong.

 The position is pinned because ListExpr carries no span of its own, so
 the diagnostic borrows the first element's. A code-only check would still
 pass if that borrowing were lost and the span went synthetic.

